## homes — name, kind, home, as; why; how many references name it

## stays
Artifact                entity    # a type of its own
ArtifactAsset           entity    # a type of its own
ArtifactComment         entity    # a type of its own
ArtifactKind            enum      # an enum keeps its name and place (it may type a stored field)
ArtifactView            component # a type of its own
ArtifactsSetup          class     # its full name is a stored key — `Osysharp.Artifacts.ArtifactsSetup.<Field>` keys the organization's policy rules and their exceptions — and no migration line renames one
BundleFile              class     # already a member
CommentsOnArtifactsOf   policy    # a virtual or supplied policy is answered by its top-level name; it stays (design §2.3)
ReadsArtifactsOf        policy    # a virtual or supplied policy is answered by its top-level name; it stays (design §2.3)
WritesArtifactsOf       policy    # a virtual or supplied policy is answered by its top-level name; it stays (design §2.3)

## ties — nothing is guessed: each stays where it is until you pin it

## no home — nothing ties it to one of the folder's types; it stays

## could be instance — its first parameter is its home, but it is published by name, has overloads or a caller passes null, so it stays static

## could be private — every reference is inside its home; the tool never narrows, a reviewer may

